# new Headers().entries(); handedOver().next()
# Nobody knows the object that the second call answers. The program has made an iterator over headers, so the `next` that is found there may be that of its class.
# Nothing has made an iterator over the parameters of a URL: the `next` of that class is not found, and what hangs on it in the table stays out of the image.
# LIBRARY: own
# RUN: valueflow-why used-builtin=URLSearchParamsIteratorPrototypeNext used-builtin=HeadersIteratorPrototypeNext
# CHECK: used-builtin=URLSearchParamsIteratorPrototypeNext
# CHECK-NEXT: not held
# CHECK-NEXT: used-builtin=HeadersIteratorPrototypeNext
# CHECK-NOT: not held

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 name="main" kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="Headers" [isFreeName]
    v2 = Construct v1, -
    v3 = PropGet v2 key="entries"
    v4 = Call v3, v2
    v5 = PropGet v0 key="handedOver" [isFreeName]
    v6 = Call v5
    v7 = PropGet v6 key="next"
    v8 = Call v7, v6
    Return
}
